  "question": {
    "text": "Two long parallel wires carry currents <math><msub><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> such that <math><msub><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>.</mo></math> When the currents are in the same direction, the magnetic field at a point midway between the wires is <math><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If the direction of <math><msub><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is reversed, the field becomes <math><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The ratio <math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math> is",
